A revoke that took the capability it was made through goes on,
so made again after a stop it fails, where a revoke never stopped went on to the end.
A call that stops leaves its caller the capability it was made through.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a call stopped where its caller cannot make it again

diff --git a/kernel/cap.c b/kernel/cap.c
--- a/kernel/cap.c
+++ b/kernel/cap.c
@@ -257,7 +257,7 @@ bool cap_revoke_below(struct cap *root, uint32_t through, bool preempt)
          * A table slot of its process can only be cleared here, never filled, so the number still names the same slot.
          */
         const struct cap *at = slot_at(core_self()->current, through);
-        if (at == NULL || at->type == CAP_NONE) {
+        if (at == NULL) {
             return true;
         }
         if (root->child != 0 && cap_stop_here(preempt)) {
